/*!
@defgroup vbatcon VBATCON Driver
@details The MCUXpresso SDK provides APIs for MCUXpresso SDK devices' VBAT Controller operation.

The VBAT Controller (VBATCON) manages the power and reset signals of the VBAT power
mode, and includes the switching logic of the ULP32K clock domain. It also exposes
on/off button control and a small bank of general-purpose retention registers that
remain powered from the VBAT supply.

The VBATCON driver supports:
  - Configuring on/off-button behavior: long-press timeout, debounce time, turn-on
    time, PMU no-acknowledge timeout, abnormal-entry deadlock protection
  - Enabling, disabling and clearing the four event sources: emergency power-off,
    power-off, power-on and OSC32K error
  - Gating the BBSM and VBAT_LPTIMER functional clocks
  - Selecting the ULP32K clock source (FRO32K vs OSC32K) under software control
  - Reading clock-readiness status flags (OSC ready, FRO ready, OSC SCXO/TCXO stable)
  - Reading and writing the VBATCON general-purpose retention registers

*/
